{"schema":1,"kind":"decision","id":"01KXGQ000HEK08MNGT70CS8VSD","title":"Make embedded SurrealKV the default store","decision":"Use a per-user SurrealKV store for the default local path and retain NAHUALI_DB_URL as the explicit remote SurrealDB override. Route both through SurrealDB dynamic connections so the public memory contract stays shared.","alternatives":[{"option":"Keep Docker as the default","why_rejected":"It leaves the installed CLI and MCP server unable to persist memory without a checkout and service operation."},{"option":"Bundle a SurrealDB child process","why_rejected":"It adds process supervision and distribution complexity while the official Rust SDK already supports embedded persistence."}],"forcing":"A first-time user must persist memory from installed binaries without cloning the repository.","scope":["Cargo.toml","crates/nahuali-core/src/database.rs","crates/nahuali-core/src/store/**","crates/nahuali-core/src/validation.rs","crates/nahuali-cli/**","crates/nahuali-mcp/**","crates/nahuali-api/**"],"commits":["3e1d70bd5ed09f18ec3a0028299ad16c6a1aa2f4"],"author":"codex","confidence":"high","tags":[],"ts":1784046157841}

{"schema":1,"kind":"decision","id":"01KXGQ001QZ8N7ASFZF2YSV972","title":"Distribute the MCP server through OCI and the official registry","decision":"Publish a multi-architecture nahuali-mcp image to GHCR, label it with the official MCP server name, and publish server.json through GitHub OIDC. Keep GitHub release binaries as the direct local installation path.","alternatives":[{"option":"Publish crates.io first","why_rejected":"The current crates are intentionally unpublished and crates.io does not by itself create an MCP Registry install surface."},{"option":"Publish metadata before a package","why_rejected":"The official registry requires a public package or remote endpoint and would reject an unverified local binary reference."}],"forcing":"Nahuali currently appears in no MCP directory and has no registry-native installation method.","scope":["Dockerfile.mcp","server.json",".github/workflows/publish-mcp.yml","crates/nahuali-mcp/**"],"commits":["3e1d70bd5ed09f18ec3a0028299ad16c6a1aa2f4"],"author":"codex","confidence":"high","tags":[],"ts":1784046157879}

{"schema":1,"kind":"decision","id":"01KXGRZR8SYJXWPCANBDSMF42C","title":"Keep the Nahuali engine protected under FSL-1.1-MIT","decision":"Keep the full Nahuali implementation source-available under FSL-1.1-MIT. Publish interoperable contracts, benchmark cases, MCP metadata, and installable artifacts without relicensing the engine.","alternatives":[{"option":"Apache-2.0 for the entire repository","why_rejected":"It would allow competitors to commercialize the engine immediately and is not required by the official MCP Registry."}],"forcing":"Nahuali needs broad evaluation and integration without giving away its commercial differentiation.","scope":["LICENSE","README.md","compliance/licensing-faq.md","Dockerfile.mcp"],"commits":["3e1d70bd5ed09f18ec3a0028299ad16c6a1aa2f4"],"author":"codex","confidence":"high","tags":[],"ts":1784048247065}

{"schema":1,"kind":"decision","id":"01KXGTAK78XE83HBYPHR2BZWS0","title":"Build MCP images on native architectures","decision":"Publish amd64 and arm64 MCP images through Docker's maintained GitHub Builder so each Rust build runs on a native GitHub-hosted runner and the final manifest carries SBOM and provenance attestations.","alternatives":[{"option":"Build both architectures with QEMU on one x64 runner","why_rejected":"SurrealDB release compilation is memory-heavy and emulation makes the release path slower and less reliable"}],"scope":[".github/workflows/publish-mcp.yml"],"commits":["3e1d70bd5ed09f18ec3a0028299ad16c6a1aa2f4"],"author":"codex","confidence":"medium","tags":[],"ts":1784049650920}
